WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.585
Applying Purdue begins with reality, not a blank diagram.

00:00:03.585 --> 00:00:06.360
Inventory assets, document their operational functions,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.220
and map actual communication paths.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.575
Then assign levels where the model clarifies responsibility and trust.

00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:14.330
If a system performs several functions or crosses levels,

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.390
record that complexity rather than forcing a misleading label.

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.275
Use the model to design segmentation.

00:00:19.275 --> 00:00:22.080
Group systems with compatible functions and consequences,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.655
place controls at meaningful boundaries, and permit only required flows.

00:00:25.655 --> 00:00:29.220
Remote access should enter through managed services, not bypass levels.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.400
Administrative paths deserve the same scrutiny as production data because they can change

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.650
configurations and logic.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.600
Purdue also guides monitoring placement.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.690
Enterprise boundaries reveal attempted movement toward OT.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:43.620
The industrial DMZ provides visibility into cross-environment exchange.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.800
Site and control-area monitoring can identify new devices, unexpected protocols,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.910
engineering activity, and changes in normal communication.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.620
Monitoring choices must account for sensitive devices and operational traffic.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.180
During incident-response planning,

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.080
use levels to identify containment options and dependencies.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.840
Blocking a boundary may protect lower levels, but it may also interrupt identity,

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.040
reporting, or support.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.040
Plans should distinguish which functions can continue locally, what visibility remains,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.295
and who can authorize isolation or shutdown.

00:01:10.295 --> 00:01:12.935
Modern cloud, industrial Internet of Things, mobile,

00:01:12.935 --> 00:01:15.240
and vendor services challenge a simple hierarchy.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.110
Some devices communicate directly with cloud platforms.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.945
Remote operations may span sites.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:23.130
Software-defined infrastructure can shift functions dynamically.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:27.300
Extend the analysis with data-flow diagrams, identity architecture, trust boundaries,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.310
and environment-specific threat modeling.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.750
The model's value lies in disciplined reasoning.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.840
It supports segmentation, access control, monitoring, inventory, and response,

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.405
but it does not replace them.

00:01:37.405 --> 00:01:40.740
Validate every conclusion against the actual process, architecture,

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.400
and operating constraints.
